  "slug": "agentic-ai-a099",
  "summary": "Recent work couples neural models with RNA binding atlases, generative design, and ribosome profiling data to predict and rank functional RNA outcomes.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned models that take sequence, structure, or experimental data and return a prediction, ranking, or design for an RNA or RNA-acting element. Prediction examples include the ecCLIP atlas and Pythia for RBP-RNA binding and 3' UTR variant effects, LigRNA for RNA-ligand binding sites, SwinTransRNA for lncRNA, circRNA, and miRNA subcellular localization from 6-mer FCGR matrices, and RiboBA for bias-aware ORF identification across ribosome profiling protocols. Design and ranking work targets function: RNAverse generates functional RNAs, and DeSTAR's top-ranked toehold sites yield working sensors about five-fold more often. What is new is the coupling of learned models with direct functional readouts for model-proposed RNAs, evident in DeSTAR and RNAverse but not uniformly across the set. A variational quantum classifier for DNMT3A and DNMT3B flanking methylation motifs applies a related sequence-classification framing to DNA rather than RNA.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-18"
}
